================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
================================================================================

The MIT license above covers the source code in this repository
(`facenet_arch.py`, `facenet_utils.py`, `face_recognition_pipeline.ipynb`).
It does NOT cover the following third-party components, which are redistributed
here under their own terms and remain the property of their respective owners.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Pretrained model weights  (`weights/*.csv`)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Source:    OpenFace, Carnegie Mellon University
               https://github.com/cmusatyalab/openface
    Model:     nn4.small2.v1
    License:   Apache License 2.0
    Trained on CASIA-WebFace and FaceScrub (~500,000 images).

    The CSV export of these weights was produced by the Keras-OpenFace project:
               https://github.com/iwantooxxoox/Keras-OpenFace

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Network architecture
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    The Inception-style architecture implemented in `facenet_arch.py` is a
    reimplementation of the OpenFace nn4.small2 network, itself derived from
    the architecture described in:

        F. Schroff, D. Kalenichenko, and J. Philbin,
        "FaceNet: A Unified Embedding for Face Recognition and Clustering",
        CVPR 2015.  https://arxiv.org/abs/1503.03832

    Layer naming follows the OpenFace convention because those names are the
    lookup keys for the pretrained weight files.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Labeled Faces in the Wild (LFW) dataset  (`archive/`)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Source:    University of Massachusetts, Amherst
               https://vis-www.cs.umass.edu/lfw/

        G. B. Huang, M. Ramesh, T. Berg, and E. Learned-Miller,
        "Labeled Faces in the Wild: A Database for Studying Face Recognition
        in Unconstrained Environments", UMass Amherst Technical Report 07-49,
        October 2007.

    The LFW images were collected from news sources, and the individual
    photographs remain subject to the copyright of their original creators.
    This dataset is NOT covered by the MIT license above and is not owned by
    this project. Consult the LFW website above for the current terms of use.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Course assignment scaffolding
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Early versions of the weight-loading and image-encoding helpers were
    adapted from the starter code for the "Face Recognition" programming
    assignment in the DeepLearning.AI Convolutional Neural Networks course
    (Course 4, Week 4), which itself credits the Keras-OpenFace project above.
    The current implementation is a rewrite, but the layer-name manifest and
    weight-tensor shape tables necessarily match the originals, since they
    index the pretrained weight files.
